          explanation: 'The opening verse of the Rig Veda (RV 1.1.1) — the first verse of the entire Vedic corpus. Agni is invoked as the priest who conducts the sacrifice, but also as the sacrifice itself. This is the foundational verse of all Vedic tradition: fire as the mediator between the human and the divine, the purifier, the transformer. Agni is not merely physical fire but the principle of transformation itself.',
